From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <fardjad.davari2@jumbo.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 13:20:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add hook context and post-tool transform

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Enable per-turn hook context with swarm metadata and
synchronous post-tool result transformation
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 0001-candidate-pre-tool-input-transformers.patch

Patch intent:
Add a swarm context system that scopes hook invocations to the correct
process role (coordinator, worker, or internal) and swarm-enabled state.
Add synchronous post_tool_transform and detached post_tool_record hooks that
receive tool input and result JSON on stdin, with large payloads spilled to
temp files. Propagate the swarm context into spawned tool-execution tasks so
transformer hooks always see the correct coordinator or worker identity.

Why it exists:
Post-tool transformers need swarm metadata to decide whether to act (e.g., the
delegation guard only replaces oversized coordinator results, preserving worker
and internal output). Without explicit propagation, tokio::spawn lost the
task-local swarm context, causing hooks to fall back to Internal with swarm
disabled. The post_tool_record hook enables detached observability of tool
invocations and output sizes. This infrastructure is personal because the
swarm context carries blueprint metadata from the worker blueprint runtime,
which is not in upstream jcode.

Upstream integration points:
crates/jcode-base/src/hooks.rs (SwarmContext, ProcessRole, with_swarm_context,
current_swarm_context, transform_tool_result_with_files,
dispatch_post_tool_record_with_files, hook_configured), crates/jcode-app-core/
src/tool/mod.rs (Registry::execute transform invocation), crates/jcode-app-core/
src/agent/turn_execution.rs (run_once, run_once_streaming,
current_swarm_hook_context), crates/jcode-app-core/src/agent/
turn_streaming_mpsc.rs (tokio::spawn tool execution context propagation),
crates/jcode-app-core/src/server/swarm.rs (run_swarm_task worker context),
crates/jcode-config-types/src/lib.rs (HooksConfig fields),
crates/jcode-base/src/config/default_file.rs, crates/jcode-base/src/config/
env_overrides.rs, docs/HOOKS.md.

Update guidance:
Keep the swarm context scope around the complete turn lifecycle, including
streaming start and end hooks. The spawned tool-execution task in
turn_streaming_mpsc.rs must capture the swarm context before tokio::spawn and
re-scope it inside the spawned task with with_swarm_context. Worker execution
must install its explicit worker context before calling the agent, and
coordinator fallback must derive role from the session and feature state.
Preserve task isolation when changing hook dispatch. The post_tool_transform
hook is synchronous and must fail open: any error or timeout leaves the
original result unchanged.

Validation:
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- agent_turn_hook_context_tracks_coordinator_swarm_feature
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- agent_turn_hook_context_preserves_explicit_worker_scope
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- registry_execute_post_tool_transform_replaces_model_visible_result
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- registry_execute_post_tool_transform_fails_open_for_all_failure_modes
cargo test -p jcode-app-core --lib -- registry_execute_post_tool_transform_and_record_share_temp_files
cargo test -p jcode-base --lib -- swarm_context_propagates_into_spawned_task
cargo test -p jcode-base --lib -- swarm_context_lost_without_explicit_propagation_in_spawned_task
cargo test -p jcode-base --lib -- swarm_context_defaults_to_internal
cargo test -p jcode-base --lib -- swarm_context_is_scoped_to_async_future
