+### Swarm context
+
+Every hook also receives process role and swarm metadata:
+
+| Variable | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| `JCODE_HOOK_PROCESS_ROLE` | `coordinator`, `worker`, or `internal` |
+| `JCODE_HOOK_SWARM_ENABLED` | `1` when swarm execution is enabled, otherwise `0` |
+| `JCODE_HOOK_SWARM_MODE` | Configured swarm mode, when known |
+| `JCODE_HOOK_WORKER_ID` | Worker identity, when known |
+| `JCODE_HOOK_WORKER_BLUEPRINT_ID` | Worker blueprint identity, when known |
+| `JCODE_HOOK_WORKER_BLUEPRINT_NAME` | Worker blueprint name, when known |
+
+Transformer and recorder stdin envelopes include a `swarm` object with the same
+fields. Unknown optional values are explicit JSON `null`.
