 `JCODE_HOOK_STATUS`, `JCODE_HOOK_DURATION_MS`, `JCODE_HOOK_OUTPUT_BYTES` (on
 success), `JCODE_HOOK_ERROR` (on failure).
 
+### `post_tool_record`
+
+This detached observer receives a JSON envelope on stdin containing `event`,
+`session_id`, `working_dir`, `tool_name`, `tool_input`, `tool_input_file`,
+`tool_result`, `tool_result_file`, `tool_success`, `output_bytes`,
+`output_lines`, `duration_ms`, and `swarm`. Its stdout and exit status are
+ignored.
+
+When `tool_input` or `tool_result` exceeds the file threshold
+(`post_tool_transform_file_threshold`, default 4096 bytes), the full content
+is written to a temp file under `jcode-tool-payloads/<session_id>/` and the
+in-envelope field is truncated to the threshold. The `*_file` field is the
+temp file path, or `null` when the content fit inline. The `output_bytes`
+and `output_lines` fields are precomputed so the hook can record them
+without parsing the result.
+
+## Tool-result transformer: `post_tool_transform`
+
+This synchronous transformer runs after a tool succeeds and before the result
+enters model context. It receives a JSON envelope on stdin containing `event`,
+`session_id`, `working_dir`, `tool_name`, `tool_input`, `tool_input_file`,
+`tool_result`, `tool_result_file`, `output_bytes`, `output_lines`,
+`tool_success`, and `swarm`. The stdin envelope is capped at 256 KB.
+
+When `tool_input` or `tool_result` exceeds the file threshold
+(`post_tool_transform_file_threshold`, default 4096 bytes; env
+`JCODE_HOOK_POST_TOOL_TRANSFORM_FILE_THRESHOLD`), the full content is
+written to a temp file under `jcode-tool-payloads/<session_id>/` and the
+in-envelope field is truncated to the threshold. The `tool_input_file` and
+`tool_result_file` fields are the temp file paths, or `null` when the
+content fit inline. The `output_bytes` and `output_lines` fields are
+precomputed so the plugin can measure without reading the file.
+
+On each `post_tool_transform` invocation the runtime sweeps
+`jcode-tool-payloads/` for files older than the TTL
+(`tool_output_ttl_secs`, default 3600 seconds; env
+`JCODE_TOOL_OUTPUT_TTL_SECS`).
+
+On success it may print exactly `{"tool_result":"replacement"}` to stdout.
+Empty or invalid output, a missing key, non-zero exit, spawn failure, or timeout
+fails open and preserves the original result. The default timeout is 500 ms and
+can be changed with `post_tool_transform_timeout_ms`.
+
 ## Gate hook: `pre_tool`
 
 `pre_tool` runs **synchronously before every tool call** and can block it:
